+/* iOS-Madeira ml1110: the context can be gone while memory notifications still arrive.
+ *
+ * Factorio started by Steam's client (a child process) called ExitProcess, and Wine's exit then unmaps the
+ * process's memory. Every unmap reports to the invalidation tracker, which calls into the FEXCore context.
+ * By then the context object had been destroyed and its memory zeroed, so the tracker's virtual call through
+ * the context's (now null) vtable read address 0xf0 and faulted (libarm64ecfex.dll+0x12b9e8,
+ * InvalidationTracker::InvalidateIntervalInternal). Nothing handled it, the process never finished exiting,
+ * and Valve's client never saw the game end.
+ *
+ * Nothing needs invalidating once the context is gone: there is no translated code left to protect. Check the
+ * global pointer (null after the unique_ptr was destroyed) and the object's first word (the vtable, zero once
+ * the memory was recycled) before handing anything to the tracker. */
+static bool ContextIsAlive() {
+  return CTX && *reinterpret_cast<void* const*>(CTX.get()) != nullptr;
+}
